[ROCm] Do not allocate a reduce workspace within a wavefront

AllReduceNeedsWorkspace returned true above 32 reducing threads. tl::AllReduce
only touches the workspace when a step crosses a wavefront, so on wave64 targets
a 64-thread reduce allocated LDS it never used. The cost was not the LDS: the
workspace shows up as a shared access in the IR, so ThreadSync put barriers around
every such reduce. A flash attention K step on gfx90a went from 4 barriers to 2
with no kernel change, and the barrier count is what ThreadSync derives, so it
stays correct by construction. Wave32 targets are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/rocm/op/reduce.cc b/src/rocm/op/reduce.cc
